NAME
       install - copy files and set attributes

SYNOPSIS
       install [OPTION]... SOURCE DEST
       install [OPTION]... SOURCE... DIRECTORY
       install -d [OPTION]... DIRECTORY...

DESCRIPTION
       Copy files and set their permission bits; mostly used by makefiles.

OPTIONS
       -d
           treat all arguments as directory names and create them

       -D
           create all leading components of DEST

       -m MODE
           set permission mode (default 755)

       -t DIR
           copy all SOURCE arguments into DIR

       -v
           print the name of each file or directory

       -c, -C, -p, -s, -o, -g
           accepted for compatibility

EXAMPLES
       install -m 644 man.1 /usr/share/man/
       install -D prog /root/bin/prog

SEE ALSO
       cp(1), chmod(1), make(1)
